hermes v0.23.0: a delegate_task whose `tasks` array repeats one entry
spawns one child per copy, and one empty stray entry fails the whole
batch.

Symptom (som, claude-opus-5-5 via anthropic/TeamClaude): dave-hermes sent
`tasks` with the same goal 20 times (20 children hammered one TV), 3 times
(two goal-only copies + the same goal with 5 KB of context) and twice;
daniel twice; 8 of dave-hermes' 15 multi-task calls in 4 days had
repeated goals. adam lost a batch to "Task 1 is missing a 'goal'" from an
empty stray entry.

Root cause: the model. The stored tool-call arguments are one valid JSON
object with the copies inside (`{"tasks": [{...}, {...}, ...]}`), and the
Anthropic path cannot repeat array elements: the anthropic SDK's
MessageStream accumulates each tool_use block's input_json_delta and
get_final_message() returns its parsed input
(agent/chat_completion_helpers.py _call_anthropic;
relay_llm.AnthropicStreamAccumulator only appends partial_json per block
index and parses it once in finalize()); a dropped stream raises
EmptyStreamError and the request is retried from scratch, never
continued into the same block. Upstream allows identical goals on purpose
(tools/delegate_tool_tasks.py _validate_batch_tasks: best-of-N fan-outs,
#81141 follow-up) and has no dedupe; #57767 (idempotency key) is about
one call dispatched twice, not repeated entries.

Fix (tools/delegate_tool_tasks.py _collapse_duplicate_tasks, called from
delegate_task before _normalize_task_list):
- entries collapse to ONE, at the first copy's position, only when the
  normalized goal (stripped, whitespace collapsed; case kept) AND every
  other model-supplied field except `group` and `context` are equal as
  canonical JSON (toolsets, model, provider, output_schema, images, role,
  backend task params, anything else; null counts as absent). Copies with
  contexts equal after whitespace normalization collapse; copies with
  different non-empty contexts all stay; a bare copy (empty context) folds
  into the first copy carrying context ([G, G+ctxA, G+ctxB] -> G+ctxA,
  G+ctxB), or, with no context copy, into the first bare copy;
- only entirely empty entries (null, "", {}, or an object whose values are
  all empty) are dropped, while one other entry remains; a goal-less entry
  with any content (`{"context": "x"}`) still fails the batch with the
  usual "Task i is missing a 'goal'";
- not on a restart re-dispatch (`_RESUME_META` set,
  tui_gateway/session_auto_continue.py): its tasks are the original
  call's, aligned with the resume indexes `_resume_remap` maps back;
- the tool result's `note` names the dropped tasks 0-based, like
  upstream's errors ("dropped Tasks 1, 4 (same task as Task 0); dropped
  empty Task 2; 2 of 5 kept (Task <i> = 0-based index in your tasks array,
  as in errors). To run identical copies on purpose, number the goals
  ..."), prepended to any note dispatch adds, and attached to a validation
  error too;
- error `Task i` labels are mapped back to the model's original array
  (_map_task_indexes): each error string is mapped on its own, only its
  leading `Task i`, BEFORE several are joined (the all-routes-refused
  error) - never a `Task i` inside a backend message or a quoted goal. A
  partially refused task's entry keeps this run's task_index (result
  order, transcripts and async/resume bookkeeping index the collapsed
  list); its error names the original task.
Identical runs on purpose stay possible with distinct goals.

Test: tests/tools/test_delegate_task_dedup.py (20 identical -> 1 with the
positions in the note; goal-only copies + one with context -> the context
one; whitespace-equal contexts collapse, different contexts stay
separate and bare copies fold into the first context copy; different
toolsets / output_schema vs images / model / provider
/ role / backend params stay separate; group and key order don't matter;
null/{}/""/blank strays dropped; `{"context": "x"}` fails the batch;
error index maps to the original array and carries the note; only a
string's leading label maps ('boom Task 2', quoted 'a. Task 1 b' stay);
all-routes-refused errors mapped before joining; a refused entry's error
names the original task; resume path
not collapsed; JSON-string tasks collapse).
tests/tools/test_delegate_batch_validation.py's exact-duplicate case now
expects one child and the note (its case-variant case is unchanged).

